            <ArticleTitle>Intra-abdominal extravasation complicating parenteral nutrition in infants.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>F207-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two infants receiving total parenteral nutrition via a central venous catheter positioned in the inferior vena cava developed an acute abdomen secondary to extravasation of the infusate. The presence of an associated abdominal mass necessitated a laparotomy in one patient. Both infants recovered completely after the catheter had been removed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
